    "title": "pandas.Index.item — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.item#\n\n- Index.item()[source]#\n- Return the first element of the underlying data as a Python scalar. This method extracts the single element from a length-1 Series or Index and returns it as a native Python scalar type (e.g., `int` ,`float` ,`str` ).\n  - Returns:\n    - scalar\n    - The first element of Series or Index.\n  - Raises:\n    - ValueError\n    - If the data is not length = 1.\n See also \n  - `Index.values`\n  - Returns an array representing the data in the Index.\n  - `Series.head`\n  - Returns the first n rows.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1]) >>> s.item() 1 For an index: >>> s = pd.Series([1], index=[\"a\"]) >>> s.index.item() 'a'",
